cff-version: 1.2.0
title: The Rhizodynamics Robot (GROOT)
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper that
  describes the system (see preferred-citation below).
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Isaiah W.
    family-names: Taylor
    affiliation: Lead developer
repository-code: "https://github.com/the-rhizodynamics-robot"
abstract: >-
  Automated, high-throughput time-lapse imaging platform (GROOT — Generating
  Rhizodynamic Observations Over Time) for studying long-term dynamic root
  growth. Includes Arduino firmware and a Python host program for the camera
  gantry, plus a QR-code label generator for growth containers.
keywords:
  - root growth
  - plant phenotyping
  - time-lapse imaging
  - robotics
  - rhizodynamics
license: MIT
